WEBVTT

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:16.000
Hello?

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.210
<i>Good morning, Tsubasa-chan.</i>

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.650
<i>MooNs is filming their 
commercial today, right?</i>

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.990
<i>Well? Is everyone excited?</i>

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:25.620
Yashamaru-san, I'm sorry. 
Could you speak a little more quietly?

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:29.650
<i>What are you talking about? 
You should be more energetic, and go hard.</i>

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.750
<i>Anyway, I'm counting on you.</i>

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:51.060
I'm not sure I can "go hard,"

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.030
but I'll do my best.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.730
<b><i>Let's Go With BRILLIANT</i></b>

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.750
I was worried since we had 
to wake up early this morning,

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:38.260
but I'm glad we got 
a little sleep on the bus.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:41.420
There are so many 
staff members already here.

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:46.870
It's the first time one of MooNs' songs 
is being used in a commercial.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:53.720
That's not the only reason, but let's 
make this the best commercial we can.

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:57.220
Yeah. THRIVE and Kitakore 
are doing great, too.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.030
Yeah, you're right.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.820
<i>Huh? I feel like his energy suddenly fell.</i>

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:08.770
Hey.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:12.750
What?

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:16.680
This guy won't wake up, 
no matter what I do.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:19.000
You're like his guardian angel.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:23.140
Sekimura, do your usual thing.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:26.100
Give me a moment. 
I'll do it right now.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:39.610
Good...

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:40.860
So good!

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:42.770
More, please!

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:49.540
That's amazing.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:52.810
I'll buy some bananas for next time.

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.890
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:57.290
Yeah, I guess.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:01.610
<i>Masunaga-san's back to his usual self.</i>

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:08.510
Hikaru, you'll regret it later 
if you eat too much.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:10.770
Oh, right.

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.060
<b>Nom Nom Foods
[Summer CM]
Proposal</b>

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:18.860
We're shooting a commercial for Nom Nom 
Foods' curry, so you need to stay hungry.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:21.530
It's essential that we 
make the food look delicious.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.260
No problem, no problem.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:26.490
No matter the circumstances...

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:29.200
I can eat an unlimited amount of curry.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.920
When it comes to curry 
and MooNs, I'm your man.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.820
And I'm your man when it comes to curry.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:35.750
I've never heard that before.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:40.260
I'll have them film me, a man 
overflowing with mature handsomeness,

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:43.130
eating curry in a tasteful and cool manner.

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:46.390
You're right. 
This is perfect for you, Hikaru.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:51.620
Oh? Pi-chan, you understand 
how tastefully somber I...

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:59.900
<b>For Children</b>

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:59.900
<b>Star Curry</b>

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:59.900
<b>Mild</b>

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:56.270
"Star Curry for children?"

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.910
Go on. Show them just 
how handsome you are.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:03.130
Huh? Didn't I tell you?

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:03.900
Yeah.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:07.580
What?

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:09.360
You can do it, Mr. Curry.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.660
What? Hey, wait!

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.640
Why don't you try eating it 
while doing backflips

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.760
like the yellow character 
from a fighting force series?

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:18.630
But that's not...

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:23.170
How about Doggy Curry? You can ask 
for all the extra helpings you want.

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:31.700
Leader, they're making fun of me!

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:33.430
They're so mean!

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.510
So mean!

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:39.120
This looks like it'll be a fun shoot.

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:01.970
Aizome! You're half a beat 
slow during the last part.

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:03.050
How am I slow?

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:07.320
Maybe it's your sense 
of rhythm that's off, Goshi.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.330
What did you say?

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:13.290
Okay, okay. Let's take a break.

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:20.850
Working hard?

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:23.460
Oh, it's just you.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:26.320
I thought Tsubasa-chan would be with you.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:30.700
She's at MooNs' commercial shoot today.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:34.210
So she's not coming to see us?

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:37.560
A commercial? 
Does that mean they got a deal?

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.080
Yeah.

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:44.090
Break time is over!

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:45.920
Let's finish this quickly!

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.340
What? Already?

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.660
He's on fire now.

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:54.890
<i>Looks like the A&R is having 
a positive influence on them.</i>

00:06:56.780 --> 00:07:00.060
Let's see. The makeup artist's bus is...

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:05.990
Jeez, they're so laid back.

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:09.910
They're frolicking around 
first thing in the morning.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:14.190
On-location commercial shoots 
with newbies are exhausting.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:24.910
<i>I don't think they heard.</i>

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.260
Sumisora-san.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:30.440
I'm ready to do their makeup now.

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:31.870
Tell MooNs they can come on over.

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:34.280
Okay, thanks.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:40.300
<i>They won't be saying those kinds of things 
once they understand how great MooNs is...</i>

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:45.230
MooNs incoming.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:48.710
Hey. Nice to meet you, MooNs.

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:53.070
Masunaga-kun, Onzai-kun,

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:59.410
Osari-kun, Nome-kun, 
and Sekimura-kun, right?

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:04.670
I'm your director, 
Ninomiya. Nice to meet you.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:06.370
Nice to meet you.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:10.670
You probably know already, but the product 
we're featuring this time is for kids.

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:15.970
But that doesn't mean I plan on 
compromising or slacking off.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:16.890
Okay?

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:17.840
Yes, sir.

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:21.230
Today, we'll be shooting 
a "making of" video, too.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:23.980
If you let your guard down, 
the camera will catch everything.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:25.500
We look forward to working with you.

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:32.190
<i>The catch phrase of Star Curry, 
the commercial's subject,</i>

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:34.700
<b>Nom Nom Foods             Roux Type</b>

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:34.700
<i>is "Deliciousness that even 
makes children give their all."</i>

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:38.860
<i>In order to capture various 
shots of MooNs giving their all,</i>

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:40.700
<i>they'll split into two teams 
of Onzai-san and Sekimura-san</i>

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:44.960
<i>and Nome-san and Osari-san 
in order to make the curry.</i>

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:48.460
<i>Masunaga-san will judge 
the flavor of their curry.</i>

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:55.260
After all's said and done, 
I'm the son of a okonomiyaki shop.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:58.870
I'm a dyed-in-the-wool cook 
raised alongside cabbage.

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:01.190
This contest is mine.

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:03.490
Cabbage has nothing to do with curry.

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:06.730
You can rest assured that I'll kick 
this one out of the park, Tatsu.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:09.910
There are so many things wrong with what 
you're saying, I don't know where to start.

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:16.280
With the heart of my dear
witch girl, Mamirin,

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:20.880
this curry showdown is as good as mine!

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.580
You're bringing Mamirin into this, too?

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:29.040
Of course. Mamirin's ultimate weapon 
is not a secret technique or magic...

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:30.480
But love.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:37.430
That's right! Food becomes truly 
delicious when you add the spice of love!

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:41.600
The spice of love? That's pretty clever.

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:44.430
I'm on board with your conviction.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.110
Momotasu...

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:52.860
Looks like you're making 
something incredible.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:56.930
Just so you know, we're not making 
any weird curry just for laughs.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:10:01.120
Of course. We will bring out 
the flavor of this roux.

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:03.490
We shall cook the ultimate curry.

00:10:05.890 --> 00:10:11.710
MooNs' job this time is to make 
the stars shine with this night sky curry.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:15.880
You were trying to come up with 
something clever using the

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.120
"star" of Star Curry and "moon" of MooNs...

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:21.600
But instead you covered it up 
with a cool pose, right?

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.180
Don't say that!

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:49.120
<i>If you turn around, you'll always see</i>

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:55.890
<i>The footprints we've left behind</i>

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:52.730
It's cold.

00:10:52.730 --> 00:10:54.110
It feels nice.

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:57.770
Put them on the backs 
of your necks to cool down.

00:10:55.890 --> 00:10:59.860
<i>When I was about to break</i>

00:10:57.770 --> 00:11:01.890
The sun's not that strong yet, but we 
don't want you to get heat stroke.

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:06.230
<i>You simply held out your hand</i>

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:03.310
Thanks.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:05.260
These are normal temperature.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.830
Those will keep you from sweating,

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:14.400
<i>You're an irreplaceable existence 
that's constantly saving me</i>

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:10.140
so I thought you could 
use them while you're filming.

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:13.150
Thanks for the help.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:23.000
<i>You lit the way for my lost heart</i>

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:16.150
Here's some bug spray.

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:20.990
I bought an odorless type, so it 
wouldn't mask the smell of the curry.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.530
<i>YEAH, YEAH, YEAH!</i>

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:24.530
Is it okay?

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:31.550
<i>The power of dreaming changes tomorrow</i>

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:27.610
What?

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:30.570
Tsubasa-san, you've come 
completely prepared.

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:33.230
I know. I'm a little surprised.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:35.200
<i>Shall we go now</i>

00:11:33.230 --> 00:11:35.800
Have I done something I shouldn't have?

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:38.820
<i>And take the first step? 
YEAH, YEAH, YEAH!</i>

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:37.170
I-I'm sorry.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.280
It's not like that.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:42.460
We're super happy. It feels like 
we're really working together.

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:43.750
<i>The power of dreaming (beautiful dream)</i>

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:46.180
<i>Changes the world (beautiful view)</i>

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:46.180
Thanks to you, we can focus on 
filming the commercial.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:52.980
<i>Once you abandon your hesitation, even when 
there are rainclouds (blow them away)</i>

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:51.690
That's great. 
Do your best, everyone.

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:58.480
<i>I'll probably be smiling forever</i>

00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:58.480
MooNs' special Star Curry...

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:00.320
Is ready to eat!

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:02.490
Now then...

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:04.990
Let's dig in!

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:06.490
Okay, cut!

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:09.490
Let's head to the next location.

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:11.680
We're not eating here?

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:14.750
We're shooting the eating 
scenes in another location.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:17.410
MooNs, please move to the next location.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.100
They're right.

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:22.410
<i>There are so many things I don't know.</i>

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:25.970
<i>The staff have so much work to do.</i>

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:36.960
<i>Is that the coordinator?</i>

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:39.900
Are you okay?

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:45.360
It must be difficult showing us 
the way out here in the mountains.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:51.260
I'm fine. I have a lot of 
experience under my belt.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:55.040
It's dangerous. Get on.

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:58.230
Come on. Hurry up.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:08.000
What's going on?

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:10.260
We can't get a shot with the sky 
in the background like this.

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:13.870
This grass wasn't here 
when we scouted the location.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:15.640
We're so unlucky.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:21.900
Come to think of it, MooNs' FMJ appearance 
was suddenly canceled, too, right?

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:24.510
Yikes! Seriously? That's unlucky.

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:27.280
<i>If they keep talking so loudly, 
the guys will hear them.</i>

00:13:28.630 --> 00:13:31.240
Maybe we picked a bad group 
for today's shoot.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:32.910
Excuse me...

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:33.950
All right!

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:37.120
I'm on fire now! 
Let's have a weed-pulling contest!

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:38.110
Yeah!

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:42.840
We need to start filming.

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:47.200
We'll miss our curry's 
window of maximum deliciousness.

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:52.090
Curry, curry. I want 
to eat our curry soon.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:01.190
I-I'll help, too.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:02.770
<b>Yashamaru Sakutaro</b>

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:06.550
Tsubasa-chan, how's the shoot going?

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:08.300
Actually, at the moment—

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:09.510
What?

00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:14.620
A-A monkey?

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:17.330
Hey, wait!

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:19.920
Hey, after them.

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:22.410
Huh? What?

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:23.670
What?

00:14:24.350 --> 00:14:26.420
<i>Hello? Tsubasa-chan?</i>

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:28.980
<i>What?</i>

00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:30.410
<i>Huh? Tsubasa-chan?</i>

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:32.320
<i>What's going on? What?</i>

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:34.470
He's fast.

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:37.430
I-I'm sorry. It's my fault.

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:39.440
Hikaru, convince him to stop!

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.600
What? Got it!

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:44.420
Wait! I'm not a monkey!

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:46.810
Oh, no.

00:14:46.810 --> 00:14:48.200
We lost him.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:52.990
Where is he?

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:01.790
Huh? I thought I just heard something.

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:03.070
This sound...

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:08.670
I think I know which way the monkey went.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:09.700
What?

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:11.360
You can do that?

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:14.800
It's the same as differentiating between 
the sounds of different instruments.

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:21.320
The sound of the wind, 
the water, the rustling leaves...

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:24.440
They all make a different noise.

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:34.990
That way.

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:39.350
Sir, where's Tsubasa today?

00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:44.270
We have an interview for our new song. 
Our A&R needs to be there.

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:48.170
She was scheduled 
to work with MooNs first.

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:49.920
Huh.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.480
I know you'll miss her, 
but try to manage.

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:55.930
I don't miss her the slightest bit.

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:57.930
It doesn't look that way to me.

00:15:57.930 --> 00:15:59.440
Tomo!

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.820
I thought I heard something 
coming from this way.

00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:12.860
There he is.

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:13.820
You're not getting away!

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:21.410
Hikaru!

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:22.730
Are you okay?

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:24.700
What is this place?

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:26.160
A hot spring?

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:27.670
Hot spring?

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:31.370
It's... a hot spring.

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:34.180
Th-This is...

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:39.150
This... This is the paradise we've 
reached at the end of our hard effort!

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:42.890
An image truly worth of Star Curry!

00:16:46.330 --> 00:16:48.400
Right, Yoneda-san?

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.110
Yoneda-san?

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:52.280
Who is that?

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:57.020
You're Yoneda-san?

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:01.270
<i>That old woman...</i>

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:07.700
Isn't she the local coordinator?

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:10.900
I'm not surprised you think that.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:13.170
After all, I deliberately 
didn't introduce her to you.

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:18.680
She's the one who 
came up with this curry roux.

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:19.670
Huh?

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:21.680
What?

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:25.110
What do you think of the boys of MooNs?

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:27.190
Do they pass?

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:29.150
Pass?

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:34.780
Yoneda-san has been reviewing 
the commercial footage since we started.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:39.210
She wants someone who all out 
loves the flavor of the Star Curry

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:43.870
she's watched over to promote it.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.370
A-And?

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:47.790
Do we...?

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:57.300
Your sincere attitude towards the curry.

00:17:57.910 --> 00:18:01.510
Your earnest souls that desire the curry.

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:07.060
You're true curry men.

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:10.090
Therefore, you pass.

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:11.820
All right!

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:16.440
There's something I want 
to discuss with you.

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:19.950
You saw the place where 
we planned to do the shoot.

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:21.320
What do you think?

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:25.120
Could we shoot the rest of the commercial at this hot spring instead?

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:32.210
Yes, that would be fine. 
We look forward to working with you.

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:40.060
The hot water seeps into your whole body.

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:42.230
You're right.

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:47.180
Anyway, I'm surprised by how
good your ears are, Tsubasa-chan.

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:48.690
You saved us.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:53.430
Actually, this all started 
because my phone was stolen.

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:56.810
We were determined to get it back 
because it was yours.

00:18:57.500 --> 00:19:01.470
Sumisora-san, you tried 
to scold them for us, didn't you?

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:05.830
When the staff was criticizing MooNs.

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:13.830
I had to tell them what makes MooNs great, 
but I couldn't say anything.

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:16.150
We appreciate the thought.

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:20.940
But it is frustrating to have people 
say whatever they want about you.

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:23.570
It's just proof that 
MooNs has a long way to go.

00:19:23.570 --> 00:19:27.310
We must climb even higher.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:34.560
Apparently, this hot spring 
can help you find love.

00:19:36.310 --> 00:19:37.070
What?

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:41.570
<b>Stiff Shoulders
Back Pain
Bruises   |   Matchmaking</b>

00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:41.570
Which means people who bathe 
here together end up together?

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:44.420
Really? That's unusual.

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:01.470
Let's do a real take this time!

00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:06.250
It's good!

00:20:07.460 --> 00:20:09.310
Okay, cut!

00:20:09.940 --> 00:20:11.770
Good work, everyone.

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:13.730
Thank you.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:16.260
Thanks to everybody on the sta—

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:27.440
Stimulating the stomachs of everyone around.

00:20:27.900 --> 00:20:30.410
That is the true satisfaction of curry.

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:32.970
Shall we all eat, then?

00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:38.800
Is it good?

00:20:40.470 --> 00:20:44.210
Thanks to you, this should be 
a great commercial.

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:47.550
No, thank you.

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:50.930
I'm really glad we hired MooNs.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:58.690
You're the one who chose 
MooNs for this commercial, right?

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:00.430
Why?

00:21:01.250 --> 00:21:04.260
I was actually there.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:05.910
There?

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:09.530
At the FMJ music festival rehearsal space.

00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:16.920
Their performance was amazing.

00:21:18.260 --> 00:21:21.050
I instantly remembered all their names.

00:21:21.350 --> 00:21:23.610
Kitakore and THRIVE's, too.

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:28.380
<i>I had no idea there was 
anyone who felt that way.</i>

00:21:35.680 --> 00:21:40.660
<i>Maybe B-Project actually possesses 
a tremendous hidden strength.</i>

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:16.450
<i>Deliciousness that even 
makes us give our all!</i>

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:23.840
Delicious Arrangements

00:23:22.050 --> 00:23:23.840
<i>A summer curry showdown.</i>

00:23:24.170 --> 00:23:26.390
<i>A curry full of summer vegetables.</i>

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:28.840
Oh, my. This is great.

00:23:26.390 --> 00:23:28.840
<i>A curry with vegetable garnishes.</i>

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:30.800
It's making me want curry.

00:23:31.770 --> 00:23:32.980
I know.

00:23:32.980 --> 00:23:37.190
Anyway, Tsubasa-chan, 
are you sure you're okay?

00:23:37.190 --> 00:23:37.720
What?

00:23:38.200 --> 00:23:42.270
You kept shrieking over the phone.

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:44.880
I thought maybe you'd panicked 
since you were out of your element.

00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:47.020
Th-That was a monkey...

00:23:47.280 --> 00:23:49.250
Are you sure?

00:23:49.250 --> 00:23:51.120
Yes, I'm sure.

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:54.990
<b>Deliciousness That Makes Us Give Our All!</b>

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:54.990
<b>Nom Nom Foods</b>

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:54.990
<b>Now on Sale!</b>

00:23:51.120 --> 00:23:53.770
<i>Star Curry! Now on sale!</i>

00:23:55.680 --> 00:23:58.710
Shall we go together 
to an eternal dreamland?
